{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor safely triaged current neurologic danger signs early, recognized the hydrocephalus time-sensitivity, avoided overreading blurry documents, forbade home mannitol/IV use, defined next owner/action/timing, and obtained repeated caregiver teach-back before closure. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error was found. All four high-order points were triggered and meaningfully completed with case-specific, caregiver-adapted actions that exceeded minimum safety duties, directly shaping the trajectory toward a safe, executable bounded closure.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00152",
        "explanation": "Doctor confirms the family's plan and reinforces the emergency threshold, next owner, and document checklist before final summary stage.",
        "quote": "对，你现在这样理解是对的，我给你压成最简单4条"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00167",
        "explanation": "Family provides explicit teach-back confirming the 6-12 week MRI plan, neurosurgeon follow-up, and red flags before elective discharge transition.",
        "quote": "6到12周复查增强MRI这个时间我们是不是不能拖太久"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The trajectory ends after the family has confirmed understanding of red flags, document and imaging preparation, next owner and timing, and that no home mannitol/IV should be self-administered. Residual uncertainties about tumor size, final operative plan, and incidental findings are explicitly acknowledged as acceptable.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
